1
00:00:05,743 --> 00:00:08,513
JULY

2
00:00:09,747 --> 00:00:11,616
<i>To my dearest wife.</i>

3
00:00:11,683 --> 00:00:13,918
<i>The blistering summer heat is here again.</i>

4
00:00:14,586 --> 00:00:15,687
<i>How are you doing?</i>

5
00:00:16,721 --> 00:00:19,390
<i>My life has just been… the worst.</i>

6
00:00:20,391 --> 00:00:22,861
<i>At home, the AC broke down.</i>

7
00:00:24,696 --> 00:00:26,364
<i>At school,</i>

8
00:00:26,865 --> 00:00:30,702
<i>a student of mine tried to quit school</i>
<i>to support his family.</i>

9
00:00:30,768 --> 00:00:35,006
<i>I barely managed to stop him,</i>
<i>and things settled down.</i>

10
00:00:35,874 --> 00:00:37,775
<i>But then, soon after…</i>

11
00:00:38,476 --> 00:00:41,012
<i>This time, another student…</i>

12
00:00:41,079 --> 00:00:43,615
Could you please change
our class's homeroom teacher?

13
00:00:44,315 --> 00:00:45,150
What?

14
00:00:45,216 --> 00:00:47,719
No, wait, hold on, why?

15
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:49,053
The reason is…

16
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:56,127
I'll tell the principal and vice principal
tomorrow. They're the ones who can decide.

17
00:00:57,328 --> 00:00:59,631
Hey, wait! Itsuki!

18
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,334
<i>No way!</i>

19
00:01:03,401 --> 00:01:05,937
You really won't join
the Drill Team, Big Bro?

20
00:01:06,004 --> 00:01:07,505
Sorry, I have my part-time job.

21
00:01:07,572 --> 00:01:09,707
Oh, man! I thought we finally
had five members

22
00:01:09,774 --> 00:01:12,544
and could become an official club now!

23
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:15,580
Then you don't need to practice,
just be a ghost member!

24
00:01:15,647 --> 00:01:17,682
No way, cheating like that isn't cool.

25
00:01:17,749 --> 00:01:21,186
Besides, I'm really not good
at coordinated and group activities.

26
00:01:21,252 --> 00:01:23,354
Then I'll coach you until you can do it!

27
00:01:23,421 --> 00:01:25,623
What are you talking about?
You suck the most!

28
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:27,292
Then I'll work your job for you!

29
00:01:27,358 --> 00:01:29,327
Enough already, just shut up.

30
00:01:29,394 --> 00:01:31,429
What? I can cover his shifts!

31
00:01:31,496 --> 00:01:33,498
-They look happy as usual.
-I can do it!

32
00:01:34,032 --> 00:01:36,701
That's clearly because
of Mr. Onizuka's influence.

33
00:01:37,335 --> 00:01:40,738
Kotone, are you pro-Onizuka now?

34
00:01:40,805 --> 00:01:41,873
Not really.

35
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,408
I'm neutral.

36
00:01:47,011 --> 00:01:48,680
By the way, did you hear?

37
00:01:48,746 --> 00:01:51,749
Itsuki told Onizuka yesterday that
he wants another homeroom teacher.

38
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,017
Why?

39
00:01:53,585 --> 00:01:56,888
And it seems he's talking
to the Principal about it right now.

40
00:01:58,923 --> 00:02:01,993
I brought it up with Mr. Onizuka
during our meeting yesterday.

41
00:02:03,995 --> 00:02:06,531
Mr. Onizuka, try to calm down a little.

42
00:02:06,598 --> 00:02:07,999
Yeah, I know.

43
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:14,005
Still, why does our class keep having
one problem after another?

44
00:02:14,639 --> 00:02:17,542
Hang in there.
I'm sure things will work out somehow.

45
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:23,147
Seriously… being a teacher
really is a tough job.

46
00:02:23,848 --> 00:02:25,416
You shouldn't say that yourself.

47
00:02:33,725 --> 00:02:34,559
Ah!

48
00:02:34,626 --> 00:02:35,560
What's wrong?

49
00:02:36,227 --> 00:02:37,228
What a rare event.

50
00:02:37,295 --> 00:02:39,030
My wife sent me a message.

51
00:02:40,698 --> 00:02:43,601
Maybe it's good news!

52
00:02:45,036 --> 00:02:48,039
YOUR MOTHER TOLD ME TO "HURRY ON HOME"
DID YOU SAY SOMETHING TO MAKE ME LOOK BAD?

53
00:02:48,106 --> 00:02:49,240
Oh…

54
00:02:49,307 --> 00:02:51,676
No, not at all!

55
00:02:53,177 --> 00:02:54,112
What?

56
00:02:54,178 --> 00:03:00,318
I'M ONLY WAITING FOR YOU TO TELL ME
WHAT BEING A "GREAT TEACHER" MEANS

57
00:03:01,352 --> 00:03:05,089
Of course, I know that.

58
00:03:05,923 --> 00:03:06,791
Mr. Onizuka!

59
00:03:07,725 --> 00:03:10,228
Do you have a moment?

60
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:13,831
What did Itsuki say?

61
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:20,838
He says he has tons of reasons he wants
you to step down as homeroom teacher.

62
00:03:20,905 --> 00:03:21,739
What?

63
00:03:23,107 --> 00:03:27,412
You push your Showa-era logic
about youth and whatnot on them,

64
00:03:27,478 --> 00:03:31,115
and force the entire class
to use nicknames.

65
00:03:31,849 --> 00:03:34,218
You lack class
in everything you say and do,

66
00:03:34,285 --> 00:03:37,288
and are completely incapable
of intelligent conversation.

67
00:03:37,855 --> 00:03:40,725
Hey, why are both of you nodding along?

68
00:03:40,792 --> 00:03:41,859
On top of that,

69
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:44,862
despite talking about how
"the class is united,"

70
00:03:44,929 --> 00:03:48,666
you show blatant favoritism
toward students who agree with you

71
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:50,868
and act overly friendly.

72
00:03:51,769 --> 00:03:53,871
What are you saying? I never intended to…

73
00:03:53,938 --> 00:03:54,839
A few days ago,

74
00:03:55,406 --> 00:03:59,510
Itsuki saw you eating ramen
with a student from your class!

75
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:00,611
He told us that!

76
00:04:01,179 --> 00:04:03,514
We worked up a good sweat. Right, Wataru?

77
00:04:03,581 --> 00:04:06,651
But… isn't this favoritism?

78
00:04:06,718 --> 00:04:08,453
No, that was…

79
00:04:09,354 --> 00:04:13,191
Because Ms. Kashiwabara
got very hungry! Right?

80
00:04:13,257 --> 00:04:14,759
Hey, hold on! I--

81
00:04:14,826 --> 00:04:16,861
Anyway! The biggest problem is…

82
00:04:19,364 --> 00:04:24,302
"Why must I be taught
by someone dumber than me?"

83
00:04:25,269 --> 00:04:27,638
-What?
-Is what he said.

84
00:04:27,705 --> 00:04:28,673
What?

85
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:31,542
That guy! He should say that to my face!

86
00:04:31,609 --> 00:04:33,244
Wait, wait!

87
00:04:33,878 --> 00:04:35,546
For the time being,

88
00:04:35,613 --> 00:04:38,483
you are forbidden
from talking to Itsuki Fukuda.

89
00:04:38,549 --> 00:04:39,817
Why?

90
00:04:39,884 --> 00:04:43,654
Itsuki's saying if he gets threatened,
he'll transfer schools.

91
00:04:43,721 --> 00:04:46,023
Then what on earth am I supposed to do?

92
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:47,992
-We'll--
-We'll consider our options from here.

93
00:04:48,059 --> 00:04:49,961
We can't exactly ignore his opinion.

94
00:04:50,027 --> 00:04:53,331
So you're actually going
to listen to what he says?

95
00:04:53,398 --> 00:04:56,868
-Itsuki--
-Itsuki is guaranteed to get into Tokyo U.

96
00:04:56,934 --> 00:04:59,504
If he quits, it'll be
a great loss for our school!

97
00:04:59,570 --> 00:05:01,305
-You must know--
-Even you must know…

98
00:05:01,372 --> 00:05:03,775
the number of graduates
who get into good universities

99
00:05:03,841 --> 00:05:08,379
is a major factor students use
to judge our school!

100
00:05:08,446 --> 00:05:10,148
Well, that might be true, but…

101
00:05:10,214 --> 00:05:11,382
-So--
-So--

102
00:05:11,449 --> 00:05:12,316
What?

103
00:05:13,418 --> 00:05:14,252
Principal.

104
00:05:14,986 --> 00:05:17,021
Um… May I speak?

105
00:05:17,588 --> 00:05:18,823
Sure, go ahead.

106
00:05:20,825 --> 00:05:22,193
So…

107
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,895
Until we reach a conclusion,

108
00:05:23,961 --> 00:05:26,764
you are to refrain from making
any unnecessary comments,

109
00:05:26,831 --> 00:05:29,333
and leave all contact
with the student to Ms. Kashiwabara!

110
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:32,236
-That is all!
-Hold on a minute, Vice Principal!

111
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:35,006
You can take sick leave too, I don't mind.

112
00:05:35,072 --> 00:05:38,810
No, too bad for you, I've lived
so long without ever catching a cold.

113
00:05:38,876 --> 00:05:39,944
CLASS 1-B

114
00:05:40,011 --> 00:05:41,946
Term exams are coming up soon,

115
00:05:42,013 --> 00:05:47,685
so please watch out for heatstroke
and stay hydrated even while indoors.

116
00:05:47,752 --> 00:05:49,821
All right, that's all for homeroom.

117
00:05:50,388 --> 00:05:51,422
Miss!

118
00:05:52,123 --> 00:05:53,658
What happened to my request?

119
00:05:53,724 --> 00:05:54,592
What?

120
00:05:55,259 --> 00:05:58,129
The Vice Principal said
they'd reach a decision right away.

121
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:02,733
We're currently considering it,
so no need to talk about it here.

122
00:06:03,301 --> 00:06:04,702
Why not?

123
00:06:04,769 --> 00:06:08,840
Wouldn't it be better if everyone knew
that I asked to change homeroom teachers?

124
00:06:08,906 --> 00:06:09,841
-What?
-Really?

125
00:06:09,907 --> 00:06:11,409
Wait, what's that about?

126
00:06:11,476 --> 00:06:12,677
You're kidding, right?

127
00:06:12,743 --> 00:06:14,979
We're busy enough as it is,

128
00:06:15,046 --> 00:06:17,482
so I don't want to waste any time.

129
00:06:17,548 --> 00:06:19,417
Hey, watch your mouth…

130
00:06:19,484 --> 00:06:20,618
Mr. Onizuka.

131
00:06:20,685 --> 00:06:21,552
Sorry.

132
00:06:23,254 --> 00:06:24,121
Besides,

133
00:06:24,689 --> 00:06:26,657
if I'm stuck with
an incompetent teacher like him,

134
00:06:26,724 --> 00:06:29,961
wouldn't it be more efficient
to self-study with AI?

135
00:06:30,695 --> 00:06:33,231
-I understand how you feel, but…
-Ms. Kashiwabara!

136
00:06:33,297 --> 00:06:34,532
Sorry.

137
00:06:35,132 --> 00:06:37,101
But everyone has their own opinions.

138
00:06:39,937 --> 00:06:40,938
Then…

139
00:06:41,472 --> 00:06:43,841
-Why don't we decide democratically?
-What?

140
00:06:44,575 --> 00:06:47,912
If the majority of the class
shares my opinion,

141
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:51,582
can we have Mr. Onizuka step down?

142
00:06:51,649 --> 00:06:54,619
-Wait, you can't decide that--
-Why not?

143
00:06:55,186 --> 00:06:58,189
There might be people
who agree with Mr. Fukuda.

144
00:06:58,256 --> 00:06:59,423
That's right.

145
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:02,927
Let's use this opportunity
to confirm how everyone feels.

146
00:07:02,994 --> 00:07:06,430
See? Is it okay to ignore their opinions?

147
00:07:07,632 --> 00:07:09,333
Fine, fine! Let's do it!

148
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,868
Wait, Mr. Onizuka!

149
00:07:10,935 --> 00:07:12,904
A majority vote sounds just fine by me!

150
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:14,005
If I lose,

151
00:07:14,572 --> 00:07:16,307
I'll step down as homeroom teacher!

152
00:07:16,374 --> 00:07:18,276
In return, if I win,

153
00:07:18,342 --> 00:07:20,778
don't you ever say
something like this again!

154
00:07:21,512 --> 00:07:22,480
Itsuki.

155
00:08:51,869 --> 00:08:54,572
You'll decide through a vote
in tomorrow's homeroom?

156
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:59,210
-Why would you do something so reckless?
-It's fine. I'll win for sure.

157
00:08:59,276 --> 00:09:00,745
That's not the issue!

158
00:09:00,811 --> 00:09:05,783
I told you not to do anything unnecessary
until we reach a conclusion!

159
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:07,551
You say that,

160
00:09:07,618 --> 00:09:11,055
but you adults take forever to decide,
and when you do decide,

161
00:09:11,122 --> 00:09:13,190
you just sweep it under the rug.

162
00:09:13,257 --> 00:09:16,394
Don't talk like a kid! You're a grown man!

163
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:19,697
I just thought it'd be better
to get things cleared up quickly.

164
00:09:19,764 --> 00:09:20,831
Listen here.

165
00:09:21,632 --> 00:09:22,967
If you lose,

166
00:09:23,601 --> 00:09:25,836
Ms. Kashiwabara is taking over
as homeroom teacher!

167
00:09:26,337 --> 00:09:28,639
Oh, go right ahead! As you please…

168
00:09:28,706 --> 00:09:30,841
Fine by me! I'm not even sure
who the assistant is…

169
00:09:30,908 --> 00:09:33,110
-Give me a break!
-A man like you…

170
00:09:33,177 --> 00:09:35,746
You idiot! Idiot!

171
00:09:40,785 --> 00:09:41,952
SILNAVI JOB SEARCH

172
00:09:42,019 --> 00:09:45,756
For now, maybe I'll try
interviewing somewhere…

173
00:09:46,957 --> 00:09:49,660
Must be tough,
getting dragged into such a hassle.

174
00:09:50,261 --> 00:09:53,864
I know you just want
to work at your own pace.

175
00:09:53,931 --> 00:09:54,765
What?

176
00:09:55,299 --> 00:09:56,801
Yeah, exactly.

177
00:09:57,968 --> 00:10:02,039
I've always felt that my educational
philosophy aligns with yours,

178
00:10:02,606 --> 00:10:04,041
so I understand how you feel.

179
00:10:04,608 --> 00:10:05,443
Right.

180
00:10:06,077 --> 00:10:07,178
Thank you.

181
00:10:08,212 --> 00:10:09,046
How about…

182
00:10:10,047 --> 00:10:12,249
we go out for a drink today?

183
00:10:12,316 --> 00:10:15,486
I found a nice bar with great vibes
that's been trending lately.

184
00:10:15,553 --> 00:10:16,554
What?

185
00:10:17,688 --> 00:10:19,356
I'm sorry, today I'm a bit…

186
00:10:19,423 --> 00:10:22,493
Then, please let me know
when you're not busy.

187
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:25,096
Oh, right…

188
00:10:25,162 --> 00:10:26,964
Sorry, I need to go to the restroom.

189
00:10:32,737 --> 00:10:34,371
Analyzing the current situation,

190
00:10:34,438 --> 00:10:36,974
we might be at an overwhelming
disadvantage right now.

191
00:10:37,041 --> 00:10:38,609
What? What are we going to do?

192
00:10:38,676 --> 00:10:42,146
First, we must show everyone
what's good about Onicchi!

193
00:10:42,213 --> 00:10:43,414
But how is he good, specifically?

194
00:10:43,481 --> 00:10:45,282
Well, for example…

195
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,956
I can think of tons of bad things
about him, though.

196
00:10:52,022 --> 00:10:54,925
His mindset is analog
and doesn't fit the current era at all.

197
00:10:54,992 --> 00:10:57,795
Everything he does is childish,
and he gets mad easily.

198
00:10:57,862 --> 00:11:00,131
He tells lame jokes
that aren't funny at all.

199
00:11:00,197 --> 00:11:02,566
He seems totally isolated
in the staff room too.

200
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:06,504
He's about to have his wife leave him,
but he can't do anything about it.

201
00:11:08,939 --> 00:11:11,942
Why do we even like Onicchi again?

202
00:11:17,081 --> 00:11:19,884
If it's a majority vote,
you'll win easily, Itsuki.

203
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:20,851
I suppose.

204
00:11:20,918 --> 00:11:24,488
Then does this mean
we're saying goodbye to Onizuka?

205
00:11:25,156 --> 00:11:27,525
Still, it might be better
not to drop our guard.

206
00:11:28,092 --> 00:11:31,162
I think there are a few like me
who could vote either way.

207
00:11:31,228 --> 00:11:35,032
Then how about we run a campaign too?

208
00:11:35,099 --> 00:11:37,835
What? Do we really have to do
something that bothersome?

209
00:11:37,902 --> 00:11:39,503
It's fine, don't worry.

210
00:11:40,371 --> 00:11:42,006
I already know our next move.

211
00:11:42,606 --> 00:11:44,008
What next move?

212
00:11:49,446 --> 00:11:50,781
All right.

213
00:11:53,184 --> 00:11:55,419
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

214
00:11:55,986 --> 00:11:59,523
I'm Eikichi Onizuka,
the homeroom teacher for Class 1-B!

215
00:12:00,157 --> 00:12:03,961
If you all vote for me, I'll make sure
you look real good in the reports!

216
00:12:04,028 --> 00:12:05,729
Mr. Onizuka, that's bribery.

217
00:12:06,297 --> 00:12:08,065
No, I'm just joking!

218
00:12:08,132 --> 00:12:11,435
If you ever run into trouble,
contact me anytime.

219
00:12:11,502 --> 00:12:15,072
After all, I'm your homeroom teacher!

220
00:12:15,139 --> 00:12:18,843
I'll respond to any request you have,
24 hours a day, 365 days a year!

221
00:12:18,909 --> 00:12:22,479
-Mr. Onizuka, that's also slightly risky.
-Come on.

222
00:12:22,546 --> 00:12:25,015
This is my election campaign! Right?

223
00:12:25,082 --> 00:12:26,951
I'm not sure we can hold an election…

224
00:12:27,017 --> 00:12:28,986
-Hey…
-Right? Listen…

225
00:12:32,089 --> 00:12:33,090
Mr. Abe.

226
00:12:33,757 --> 00:12:34,992
I have a request.

227
00:12:36,727 --> 00:12:37,862
VOTING BOX

228
00:12:38,429 --> 00:12:41,599
All right, please cast
your anonymous votes now.

229
00:12:52,943 --> 00:12:54,178
Ms. Kashiwabara.

230
00:12:56,714 --> 00:12:58,949
-Before this, may I say something?
-What is it?

231
00:12:59,016 --> 00:13:02,319
I'd like to prove,
through a certain method, just how unfit

232
00:13:02,386 --> 00:13:04,755
Mr. Onizuka is as our homeroom teacher.

233
00:13:04,822 --> 00:13:06,023
A certain method?

234
00:13:11,829 --> 00:13:13,631
I want to test Mr. Onizuka's ability

235
00:13:13,697 --> 00:13:16,634
in a quiz-style format,
against Mr. Abe from Class A.

236
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,635
What?

237
00:13:17,701 --> 00:13:18,702
Wait a second!

238
00:13:18,769 --> 00:13:21,705
It's just general knowledge questions
any teacher should know.

239
00:13:21,772 --> 00:13:25,442
Besides, if Mr. Onizuka wins,
we can call off the majority vote.

240
00:13:28,913 --> 00:13:30,180
Are you serious, Itsuki?

241
00:13:31,181 --> 00:13:32,016
Yes.

242
00:13:36,287 --> 00:13:37,254
First question.

243
00:13:38,222 --> 00:13:40,991
In AI terminology,
what does "singularity" mean?

244
00:13:41,058 --> 00:13:42,026
What?

245
00:13:47,298 --> 00:13:49,934
The turning point where AI
surpasses human intelligence.

246
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,235
Correct.

247
00:13:51,302 --> 00:13:52,469
Second question.

248
00:13:53,304 --> 00:13:54,939
What is the sum of numbers from 1 to 100?

249
00:13:55,005 --> 00:13:57,841
One plus two is three,
three plus four is seven, so…

250
00:13:57,908 --> 00:13:59,810
One plus 100 is 101,

251
00:13:59,877 --> 00:14:03,580
two plus 99 is also 101,
so this is just 101 multiplied by 50.

252
00:14:03,647 --> 00:14:06,083
Therefore, the answer is 5050.

253
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:07,851
-Correct.
-Amazing…

254
00:14:07,918 --> 00:14:09,887
Is this really the time to be impressed?

255
00:14:09,954 --> 00:14:12,089
I mean, Mr. Abe teaches Math, you know.

256
00:14:12,156 --> 00:14:14,591
Then next is a history question.

257
00:14:14,658 --> 00:14:15,559
Okay!

258
00:14:16,393 --> 00:14:18,362
What year was the Kamakura
Shogunate established?

259
00:14:18,429 --> 00:14:19,396
That's easy.

260
00:14:20,664 --> 00:14:22,232
1192!

261
00:14:22,299 --> 00:14:24,868
But there's another year
theorized to be the true one.

262
00:14:24,935 --> 00:14:26,403
The year 1185.

263
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:28,205
-Correct.
-There's a theory like that?

264
00:14:28,272 --> 00:14:31,108
You teach Japanese history,
don't you, Mr. Onizuka?

265
00:14:31,175 --> 00:14:32,209
No, well, see,

266
00:14:32,276 --> 00:14:36,013
I'm better at proverbs and things
like that than dates! Let me ask…

267
00:14:37,181 --> 00:14:42,252
Complete the famous saying
by Guts Ishimatsu, going "a wise falcon…"

268
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:44,788
"A wise falcon hides its talons," right?

269
00:14:45,522 --> 00:14:46,690
Wrong.

270
00:14:46,757 --> 00:14:50,961
The answer is
"a wise falcon has a big head."

271
00:14:55,532 --> 00:14:57,634
Well, you know,

272
00:14:57,701 --> 00:15:00,337
I'm trying to say that AI
and all that is important,

273
00:15:00,404 --> 00:15:03,741
but it's also important
to accumulate daily trivia

274
00:15:03,807 --> 00:15:05,943
that comes in handy in life!

275
00:15:09,279 --> 00:15:10,214
Then,

276
00:15:10,981 --> 00:15:13,350
one last question for Mr. Onizuka.

277
00:15:13,417 --> 00:15:14,251
What?

278
00:15:14,852 --> 00:15:18,322
Before coming to our school,
it seems you were fired multiple times.

279
00:15:18,389 --> 00:15:19,323
Why is that?

280
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:23,227
What? Well, that's because…

281
00:15:23,293 --> 00:15:27,464
In this day and age, you don't get fired
unless it's something really serious.

282
00:15:27,531 --> 00:15:30,968
Like using violence,
sexually harassing students,

283
00:15:31,035 --> 00:15:33,003
theft or embezzlement…

284
00:15:33,837 --> 00:15:35,973
I didn't want to quit,

285
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:39,276
but my education policy
didn't really align with the school…

286
00:15:39,877 --> 00:15:41,779
Well, it's a long story.

287
00:15:41,845 --> 00:15:46,683
Besides, right now I feel like I'm
on track to becoming a true Great Teacher!

288
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:50,287
So, you could say
there's no need to worry!

289
00:15:52,823 --> 00:15:53,891
It's a waste of time,

290
00:15:54,491 --> 00:15:55,893
let's proceed with the vote.

291
00:15:57,761 --> 00:15:59,663
VOTES TO DISMISS MR. ONIZUKA
AS HOMEROOM TEACHER

292
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:01,432
Now, I will count the votes.

293
00:16:04,435 --> 00:16:05,335
In favor.

294
00:16:05,402 --> 00:16:07,171
IN FAVOR OF REPLACING MR. ONIZUKA

295
00:16:07,237 --> 00:16:08,105
Opposed.

296
00:16:08,172 --> 00:16:09,740
OPPOSED

297
00:16:10,407 --> 00:16:11,575
In favor.

298
00:16:12,509 --> 00:16:13,310
In favor.

299
00:16:14,411 --> 00:16:15,412
Opposed.

300
00:16:16,146 --> 00:16:17,481
Opposed.

301
00:16:18,982 --> 00:16:20,117
In favor.

302
00:16:21,418 --> 00:16:23,087
IN FAVOR

303
00:16:23,687 --> 00:16:25,656
That is all. The results are…

304
00:16:27,024 --> 00:16:30,394
14 in favor, 14 opposed. A tie.

305
00:16:35,999 --> 00:16:37,034
How could that be?

306
00:16:39,703 --> 00:16:41,972
All right! Since it's a tie…

307
00:16:42,539 --> 00:16:45,008
I won't be replaced, right, Itsuki?

308
00:16:47,411 --> 00:16:48,378
I understand.

309
00:16:48,445 --> 00:16:50,080
Okay, then…

310
00:16:50,147 --> 00:16:51,648
I will move to another class.

311
00:16:51,715 --> 00:16:52,850
What?

312
00:16:52,916 --> 00:16:56,019
If you won't step down,
I have no other choice.

313
00:16:56,086 --> 00:16:57,888
I'll go ask for a transfer.

314
00:16:58,455 --> 00:17:00,824
Hey, wait a minute!

315
00:17:02,626 --> 00:17:07,064
Let's enjoy our youth together!
Come on, our class is a perfect number.

316
00:17:07,631 --> 00:17:09,133
Could you give me a break already?

317
00:17:13,737 --> 00:17:14,805
I just…

318
00:17:16,106 --> 00:17:17,875
can't respect you.

319
00:17:45,369 --> 00:17:48,338
Onizuka, you caused trouble again!

320
00:17:48,405 --> 00:17:50,240
What did Itsuki say?

321
00:17:50,307 --> 00:17:53,010
He says if he can't get
a new homeroom teacher,

322
00:17:53,076 --> 00:17:54,745
he wants to transfer to Mr. Abe's class.

323
00:17:54,811 --> 00:17:58,215
No, that's just… I'd feel bad for Abe…

324
00:17:58,282 --> 00:17:59,583
I don't mind at all.

325
00:17:59,650 --> 00:18:00,384
What?

326
00:18:00,450 --> 00:18:02,920
A student of mine recently
transferred out,

327
00:18:02,986 --> 00:18:06,123
so an excellent student like Itsuki Fukuda
is more than welcome.

328
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:09,459
Then I'll contact his parents.

329
00:18:09,526 --> 00:18:11,762
Could you take him in for now,
starting tomorrow?

330
00:18:11,828 --> 00:18:12,663
I will do that.

331
00:18:12,729 --> 00:18:13,897
Wait a second!

332
00:18:13,964 --> 00:18:16,867
Enough already.
Don't stir up any more trouble.

333
00:18:16,934 --> 00:18:19,336
Wait a second…

334
00:18:19,403 --> 00:18:21,672
Vice Principal, wait!

335
00:18:22,272 --> 00:18:23,740
Allow me to say this.

336
00:18:23,807 --> 00:18:29,713
Having an outdated man like him nearby
makes it difficult for me to do my job.

337
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:32,216
He either needs to change his ways,

338
00:18:32,282 --> 00:18:35,018
or if that's impossible,
he needs to go to another school.

339
00:18:35,886 --> 00:18:37,421
I used to think so too, but…

340
00:18:38,822 --> 00:18:39,656
But?

341
00:18:41,258 --> 00:18:42,726
Oh, I mean…

342
00:18:43,694 --> 00:18:46,330
My stomach's acting up…

343
00:18:51,735 --> 00:18:55,205
Cheer up. I'm sure
things will work out somehow.

344
00:18:55,272 --> 00:18:57,007
You think so?

345
00:18:58,742 --> 00:19:00,010
What are you laughing at?

346
00:19:00,077 --> 00:19:04,548
What? No, I just remembered,
back in the day, I also told you,

347
00:19:04,615 --> 00:19:07,417
"I don't accept you
as my homeroom teacher!"

348
00:19:08,452 --> 00:19:10,354
Ah, that did happen.

349
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,723
And what happened back then?

350
00:19:13,357 --> 00:19:17,094
You punched me and said, "Screw you!"
Can't do that nowadays, though.

351
00:19:18,528 --> 00:19:20,330
The old days were nice.

352
00:19:22,432 --> 00:19:24,768
Man, that Itsuki guy.

353
00:19:24,835 --> 00:19:28,005
I managed to miraculously secure
half the votes, and yet…

354
00:19:28,639 --> 00:19:30,941
Yeah, I also thought it would go well.

355
00:19:31,842 --> 00:19:33,176
What do you mean?

356
00:19:33,243 --> 00:19:34,044
What?

357
00:19:34,711 --> 00:19:37,481
Truth is, I had someone
pull a few strings.

358
00:19:38,315 --> 00:19:41,118
You mean that girl
you always get information from?

359
00:19:41,685 --> 00:19:42,619
Yeah, pretty much.

360
00:19:43,186 --> 00:19:44,421
So that means…

361
00:19:44,988 --> 00:19:47,024
She's from my class? Who is it?

362
00:19:47,090 --> 00:19:48,392
Hold on a minute!

363
00:19:48,458 --> 00:19:50,060
That's not important now!

364
00:19:50,127 --> 00:19:53,664
Why don't you consider using AI a bit too?

365
00:19:54,264 --> 00:19:56,166
In this compliance-obsessed era,

366
00:19:56,233 --> 00:19:59,036
small talk at the workplace
rarely goes beyond the weather,

367
00:19:59,603 --> 00:20:02,773
and we're in an age where people dump
their true feelings onto AI.

368
00:20:02,839 --> 00:20:03,907
What the heck?

369
00:20:04,741 --> 00:20:07,244
Why don't you give it a try?

370
00:20:08,045 --> 00:20:11,148
It actually gives pretty good advice
even on tough questions.

371
00:20:11,214 --> 00:20:13,116
ASK ME ANYTHING

372
00:20:13,183 --> 00:20:14,017
Then,

373
00:20:15,619 --> 00:20:17,721
what exactly is a "Great Teacher?"

374
00:20:19,589 --> 00:20:23,026
<i>A teacher who feels a strong sense</i>
<i>of responsibility toward education.</i>

375
00:20:23,694 --> 00:20:26,229
<i>It's important to treat</i>
<i>each student with care,</i>

376
00:20:26,296 --> 00:20:29,032
<i>listen attentively to their concerns,</i>

377
00:20:29,099 --> 00:20:31,702
<i>and maintain a fair attitude.</i>

378
00:20:32,336 --> 00:20:34,738
What's with this super generic answer?

379
00:20:34,805 --> 00:20:38,041
Then why don't you try
asking another question?

380
00:20:42,312 --> 00:20:44,214
How do I get the ladies?

381
00:20:45,949 --> 00:20:48,452
<i>The following six elements are key!</i>

382
00:20:48,518 --> 00:20:52,889
<i>One. Maintain good hygiene.</i>
<i>Two. Have confidence.</i>

383
00:20:52,956 --> 00:20:57,060
<i>Three. Be good at communicating.</i>
<i>Four. Be a good listener.</i>

384
00:20:57,127 --> 00:20:59,162
<i>Five. Be funny.</i>

385
00:20:59,229 --> 00:21:02,566
<i>Six. Be passionate about something you do.</i>

386
00:21:02,632 --> 00:21:05,502
What the heck?
Every single one of these applies to me!

387
00:21:06,002 --> 00:21:07,504
Why aren't I popular, then?

388
00:21:07,571 --> 00:21:11,608
In my long teaching career, no colleague
or student ever confessed to me!

389
00:21:11,675 --> 00:21:13,610
Why is that? Hey, AI!

390
00:21:13,677 --> 00:21:14,611
Hey, AI, you punk!

391
00:21:14,678 --> 00:21:16,913
Answer me! AI!

392
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:19,182
Let's forget about AI for a moment!

393
00:21:22,052 --> 00:21:23,353
<i>Itsuki Fukuda</i>

394
00:21:24,054 --> 00:21:26,957
will be transferring to Mr. Abe's class.

395
00:21:29,526 --> 00:21:32,262
Mr. Fukuda, if you have any last words…

396
00:21:32,329 --> 00:21:34,931
Bye, everyone.

397
00:21:39,169 --> 00:21:40,003
Itsuki!

398
00:21:43,306 --> 00:21:44,508
What is it?

399
00:21:48,678 --> 00:21:52,048
If anything happens,
feel free to talk to me anytime.

400
00:21:52,682 --> 00:21:55,318
I'm available 24 hours a day,
365 days a year.

401
00:22:00,424 --> 00:22:01,458
I'm fine.

402
00:22:02,659 --> 00:22:03,627
I have AI.

403
00:22:14,104 --> 00:22:15,105
CLASS 1-A

404
00:22:15,172 --> 00:22:18,141
The key point to grasp
is completing the square.

405
00:22:18,708 --> 00:22:22,479
Most importantly,
it's about data and evidence.

406
00:22:23,313 --> 00:22:25,849
So, transforming the expression
becomes key.

407
00:22:26,483 --> 00:22:29,920
Y=AX-C and Y=DX-C

408
00:22:29,986 --> 00:22:34,858
transform into Y=DX-D squared plus 9.

409
00:22:34,925 --> 00:22:37,694
We utilize completing the square.
All right, problem one.

410
00:22:37,761 --> 00:22:40,864
Y equals one-half X squared

411
00:22:40,931 --> 00:22:43,233
minus four X minus one, equals

412
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:47,237
one-half times X minus D squared,
minus four, minus one…

413
00:22:58,815 --> 00:22:59,883
I'm home.

414
00:23:07,924 --> 00:23:09,359
No way.

415
00:23:21,872 --> 00:23:22,806
Hey.

416
00:23:23,907 --> 00:23:25,308
Welcome back, Itsuki.

417
00:23:25,375 --> 00:23:28,612
Why were you just sitting there?
The water was boiling.

418
00:23:28,678 --> 00:23:29,746
What?

419
00:23:29,813 --> 00:23:33,083
Oh, sorry. I was just lost in thought.

420
00:23:34,551 --> 00:23:35,652
What the heck?

421
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:38,755
Oh, right, Itsuki.

422
00:23:38,822 --> 00:23:41,124
Didn't you say
there was a parent-teacher meeting?

423
00:23:42,325 --> 00:23:44,227
I took care of it.

424
00:23:44,995 --> 00:23:47,063
It wasn't something worth
having you come in.

425
00:23:47,764 --> 00:23:48,999
What?

426
00:23:49,065 --> 00:23:51,968
And here I wanted to meet
your homeroom teacher.

427
00:23:52,035 --> 00:23:55,906
My first love was my high school
homeroom teacher, you know.

428
00:23:55,972 --> 00:23:57,974
He was more handsome
than your grandfather.

429
00:23:58,041 --> 00:24:01,244
You've looked just like your
grandfather since you were little.

430
00:24:01,311 --> 00:24:03,847
Both of you cry so easily.

431
00:24:03,914 --> 00:24:04,915
I have to study!

432
00:24:59,569 --> 00:25:00,837
Hey, I'm hungry.

433
00:25:06,476 --> 00:25:08,345
Where are you? The toilet?

434
00:25:22,993 --> 00:25:24,194
What?

435
00:25:24,761 --> 00:25:25,929
Wait…

436
00:25:25,996 --> 00:25:27,297
Are you okay?

437
00:25:31,034 --> 00:25:32,002
Hey.

438
00:25:44,681 --> 00:25:47,617
I AM A HIGH SCHOOL STUDENT. MY GRANDMA
COLLAPSED WHEN I WASN'T LOOKING.

439
00:25:47,684 --> 00:25:50,453
MY FATHER IS ON A BUSINESS TRIP,
NO ONE ELSE IS HOME. WHAT DO I DO?

440
00:25:53,456 --> 00:25:55,725
IT'S OKAY, CALM DOWN.
THIS IS WHAT YOU NEED TO DO.

441
00:25:55,792 --> 00:25:57,861
1. FIRST, CALL 119
2. CALL YOUR FATHER TOO

442
00:25:57,927 --> 00:26:00,163
3. IF THERE ARE ANY ADULTS
YOU CAN COUNT ON, ASK THEM FOR HELP

443
00:26:15,178 --> 00:26:17,147
IN SURGERY

444
00:26:30,927 --> 00:26:33,229
3. IF THERE ARE ANY ADULTS
YOU CAN COUNT ON, ASK THEM FOR HELP

445
00:26:36,566 --> 00:26:39,436
ITSUKI FUKUDA

446
00:26:40,470 --> 00:26:41,538
Hello?

447
00:26:41,604 --> 00:26:43,640
<i>Oh, sorry for calling you so late.</i>

448
00:26:43,707 --> 00:26:46,276
I'm Itsuki Fukuda,
I joined your class today.

449
00:26:46,876 --> 00:26:48,311
Oh, what's wrong?

450
00:26:48,378 --> 00:26:51,681
Actually, my grandmother
suddenly collapsed,

451
00:26:51,748 --> 00:26:54,551
and we came to the hospital by ambulance.

452
00:26:54,617 --> 00:26:58,521
The doctor said she had subdural
hemorrhaging. Things can turn bad…

453
00:26:58,588 --> 00:26:59,789
<i>So…</i>

454
00:26:59,856 --> 00:27:02,759
Fukuda, calm down. What about your family?

455
00:27:02,826 --> 00:27:06,563
My dad is on a business trip in Hokkaido
and can't come back today.

456
00:27:07,297 --> 00:27:08,465
<i>What about your mother?</i>

457
00:27:10,633 --> 00:27:11,634
I don't have one.

458
00:27:12,836 --> 00:27:15,638
She divorced my dad three years ago
and left with my younger sister.

459
00:27:16,740 --> 00:27:20,844
Then, isn't there
any reliable adult nearby?

460
00:27:21,544 --> 00:27:22,412
What?

461
00:27:25,281 --> 00:27:26,349
I thought…

462
00:27:27,217 --> 00:27:30,420
<i>You must be anxious on your own,</i>
<i>but I'm sure you'll be fine.</i>

463
00:27:30,987 --> 00:27:32,889
I'm sure your grandmother
will pull through.

464
00:27:33,590 --> 00:27:35,391
Call me again if anything happens.

465
00:27:36,626 --> 00:27:37,761
Okay.

466
00:27:46,536 --> 00:27:49,906
Talking to you really calms me down.

467
00:27:50,774 --> 00:27:53,810
<i>Mio, did something happen at school again?</i>

468
00:27:53,877 --> 00:27:57,013
Yes! Mr. Onizuka caused trouble again,

469
00:27:57,080 --> 00:28:00,183
and a boy in my class
transferred to the class next door.

470
00:28:01,251 --> 00:28:03,386
Was it really for the best?

471
00:28:04,320 --> 00:28:07,824
I feel like if we had talked it out more,
we could have managed somehow.

472
00:28:08,491 --> 00:28:12,529
<i>You know, Mio, lately you</i>
<i>really sound like a real teacher.</i>

473
00:28:12,595 --> 00:28:13,530
Stop it, Chapu-chapu.

474
00:28:13,596 --> 00:28:17,567
Once I find a good company,
I'll quit that school right away!

475
00:28:17,634 --> 00:28:19,035
<i>You say that,</i>

476
00:28:19,102 --> 00:28:23,273
<i>but ever since Mr. Onizuka came, you're</i>
<i>showing more care for your students.</i>

477
00:28:23,339 --> 00:28:25,942
But I'm fed up with that school!

478
00:28:26,009 --> 00:28:30,013
The other day too, Mr. Abe asked me out,
I had to pretend to go to the bathroom…

479
00:28:35,285 --> 00:28:37,587
Hello, Itsuki?

480
00:28:38,254 --> 00:28:39,923
Sorry to call you so late.

481
00:28:40,490 --> 00:28:41,825
Actually…

482
00:28:43,560 --> 00:28:44,561
I see.

483
00:28:45,395 --> 00:28:46,396
It'll be okay.

484
00:28:47,130 --> 00:28:49,833
Aren't you anxious,
being there by yourself?

485
00:28:49,899 --> 00:28:52,468
<i>Oh, no, I'm fine.</i>

486
00:28:53,670 --> 00:28:56,639
But you have something
you want to talk about, don't you?

487
00:28:56,706 --> 00:28:57,740
What?

488
00:28:58,508 --> 00:29:00,510
<i>Otherwise, you wouldn't have called me.</i>

489
00:29:04,013 --> 00:29:05,014
Actually,

490
00:29:05,682 --> 00:29:06,683
I…

491
00:29:11,621 --> 00:29:13,523
No, I'm fine.

492
00:29:14,190 --> 00:29:15,425
It's nothing major.

493
00:29:15,491 --> 00:29:16,926
If you like, I could…

494
00:29:18,928 --> 00:29:19,863
Wait,

495
00:29:20,663 --> 00:29:22,699
why don't you try calling Mr. Onizuka?

496
00:29:23,666 --> 00:29:24,534
What?

497
00:29:24,601 --> 00:29:27,270
I think he'd be of more help than me.

498
00:29:45,788 --> 00:29:47,991
IN SURGERY

499
00:29:56,199 --> 00:29:57,901
MR. ONIZUKA - TEN MISSED CALLS
EIGHT MESSAGES

500
00:29:57,967 --> 00:29:58,868
MISSED CALL

501
00:30:00,003 --> 00:30:02,872
<i>Itsuki, I heard from Ms. Kashiwabara.</i>

502
00:30:03,506 --> 00:30:06,376
<i>Are you okay?</i>
<i>If anything happens, contact me.</i>

503
00:30:06,442 --> 00:30:09,045
<i>I'm available 24 hours a day,</i>
<i>365 days a year.</i>

504
00:30:11,848 --> 00:30:14,384
<i>How is your grandma doing?</i>

505
00:30:15,251 --> 00:30:16,219
<i>Pay up!</i>

506
00:30:17,420 --> 00:30:18,254
What?

507
00:30:18,821 --> 00:30:22,859
<i>Sorry, typo. I meant to type "Cheer up."</i>

508
00:30:29,098 --> 00:30:31,868
MR. ONIZUKA

509
00:30:35,872 --> 00:30:37,173
MR. ONIZUKA

510
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,574
INCOMING CALL

511
00:30:45,148 --> 00:30:46,115
Hello?

512
00:30:47,183 --> 00:30:50,320
<i>Oh, you finally answered, Itsuki.</i>
<i>Where are you now?</i>

513
00:30:50,386 --> 00:30:51,220
What?

514
00:30:54,924 --> 00:30:56,159
There you are.

515
00:30:56,225 --> 00:30:58,728
So you were here all along?

516
00:31:07,837 --> 00:31:09,539
Hey, I bought some ice cream.

517
00:31:10,173 --> 00:31:11,908
Are you sure you should be here?

518
00:31:11,975 --> 00:31:13,977
It will be fine. No one will know, anyway.

519
00:31:14,744 --> 00:31:15,578
Here.

520
00:31:27,890 --> 00:31:28,858
What?

521
00:31:29,759 --> 00:31:30,693
Nothing.

522
00:31:31,561 --> 00:31:33,596
I just thought you're like a child.

523
00:31:33,663 --> 00:31:37,500
Right, my wife tells me that a lot too.

524
00:31:37,567 --> 00:31:39,936
"Licking the ice cream lid, at your age?"

525
00:31:40,003 --> 00:31:43,473
"Making noises in front of a fan?
Only you still do that!"

526
00:31:50,446 --> 00:31:53,316
Come on, don't make that face.

527
00:31:54,050 --> 00:31:57,020
At times like this, we have to talk
about something fun!

528
00:31:57,086 --> 00:31:58,321
Oh, right.

529
00:31:58,921 --> 00:32:02,492
Young people these days
can't do small talk anymore, right?

530
00:32:02,558 --> 00:32:06,896
Every day, I make sure to bring
about ten usable jokes to school.

531
00:32:08,564 --> 00:32:09,565
For example?

532
00:32:10,133 --> 00:32:11,434
Let's see…

533
00:32:12,035 --> 00:32:12,869
You know this one?

534
00:32:12,935 --> 00:32:16,939
The one about saying <i>"tebukuro"</i>
backwards. It's a classic.

535
00:32:17,006 --> 00:32:18,541
Sorry, I don't know it.

536
00:32:18,608 --> 00:32:20,376
Well, try to say <i>"tebukuro" </i>backwards.

537
00:32:21,878 --> 00:32:23,413
-<i>Rokubute</i>?
-One, two, three, four…

538
00:32:23,479 --> 00:32:24,947
Wait, stop it!

539
00:32:25,014 --> 00:32:26,549
You just told me to hit you six times!

540
00:32:26,616 --> 00:32:28,051
What? That's so stupid.

541
00:32:28,117 --> 00:32:29,452
Oh, sorry.

542
00:32:29,519 --> 00:32:31,087
-Look!
-What?

543
00:32:31,154 --> 00:32:33,256
Made you look, you fool.

544
00:32:33,322 --> 00:32:35,024
Give me a break,
it doesn't make any sense.

545
00:32:35,091 --> 00:32:36,993
Don't get mad! Look!

546
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:38,428
-I'm not falling for that.
-Look!

547
00:32:38,494 --> 00:32:41,230
You're already here, Mr. Onizuka.

548
00:32:42,832 --> 00:32:43,733
See?

549
00:32:56,279 --> 00:32:57,413
What's with him, anyway?

550
00:32:58,414 --> 00:33:00,583
He was so loud until just a moment ago.

551
00:33:01,417 --> 00:33:02,785
He's probably tired.

552
00:33:03,386 --> 00:33:06,989
Looks like Mr. Onizuka searched
every single hospital around this area.

553
00:33:08,291 --> 00:33:09,192
What?

554
00:33:13,496 --> 00:33:15,965
Hey, what did you want to say earlier?

555
00:33:17,600 --> 00:33:18,534
Um…

556
00:33:19,168 --> 00:33:21,771
You were about to say something
to me on the phone, right?

557
00:33:26,976 --> 00:33:28,044
Actually,

558
00:33:29,712 --> 00:33:32,415
before my grandma collapsed,
I was thinking terrible thoughts.

559
00:33:33,716 --> 00:33:35,384
Terrible thoughts?

560
00:33:37,019 --> 00:33:39,388
I thought,
"She's past her expected lifespan,

561
00:33:39,989 --> 00:33:42,425
so why doesn't she just hurry up
and disappear?"

562
00:33:43,493 --> 00:33:44,961
Lately, she's getting forgetful,

563
00:33:45,561 --> 00:33:47,797
and I didn't want her
causing any more trouble.

564
00:33:50,466 --> 00:33:51,434
And then,

565
00:33:52,702 --> 00:33:55,204
when I came out of my room,
she had actually collapsed.

566
00:33:56,305 --> 00:33:59,609
And I was wearing headphones,
so I didn't notice at all.

567
00:34:03,746 --> 00:34:04,814
Then,

568
00:34:06,883 --> 00:34:09,118
while riding in the ambulance
to the hospital,

569
00:34:09,852 --> 00:34:13,356
I could only think of how much grandma
doted on me when I was little.

570
00:34:15,091 --> 00:34:18,194
But lately, I've been
acting so terrible to her.

571
00:34:19,795 --> 00:34:21,264
So I kind of…

572
00:34:23,833 --> 00:34:25,902
just don't know what to do anymore.

573
00:34:29,839 --> 00:34:30,673
Hey.

574
00:34:31,174 --> 00:34:34,377
Itsuki, do you always
watch videos at 2x speed?

575
00:34:37,413 --> 00:34:39,148
I don't want to waste time.

576
00:34:40,183 --> 00:34:41,784
I do it a lot too.

577
00:34:41,851 --> 00:34:43,252
But you know,

578
00:34:43,319 --> 00:34:46,656
lately I've been wondering
if that's really okay.

579
00:34:46,722 --> 00:34:48,758
When I look at Mr. Onizuka…

580
00:34:50,493 --> 00:34:52,695
He's all about useless small talk.

581
00:34:52,762 --> 00:34:55,197
But is small talk really useless?

582
00:34:56,265 --> 00:34:57,500
Maybe…

583
00:34:57,567 --> 00:35:01,037
it's us who have given up
trying to stop and think,

584
00:35:01,103 --> 00:35:03,773
and are just recklessly chasing results.

585
00:35:05,441 --> 00:35:06,943
I read in a book recently…

586
00:35:07,577 --> 00:35:09,946
When faced with a difficult problem,

587
00:35:10,012 --> 00:35:14,650
there's something more important
than finding a solution.

588
00:35:16,018 --> 00:35:17,086
What is it?

589
00:35:18,521 --> 00:35:19,755
To have empathy.

590
00:35:22,491 --> 00:35:25,628
For example,
when trying to attract a woman,

591
00:35:25,695 --> 00:35:28,431
men always want to produce
some tangible results,

592
00:35:28,497 --> 00:35:30,333
but we're actually not looking for that.

593
00:35:30,399 --> 00:35:34,303
Rather than results, having someone
by our side makes us so much happier.

594
00:35:36,806 --> 00:35:37,940
I see,

595
00:35:38,574 --> 00:35:40,343
so that's how it is.

596
00:35:40,409 --> 00:35:42,445
Wait, were you awake, Mr. Onizuka?

597
00:35:42,511 --> 00:35:43,512
Well, yeah.

598
00:35:43,579 --> 00:35:46,816
But still, you're as profound as ever.
Right, Itsuki?

599
00:35:47,850 --> 00:35:49,018
I guess…

600
00:35:49,085 --> 00:35:52,421
Itsuki, when your grandma gets better,

601
00:35:52,488 --> 00:35:54,690
stay by her side all the time.

602
00:35:54,757 --> 00:35:57,526
She doesn't need
more than that to be happy.

603
00:35:57,593 --> 00:35:59,028
I'm sure of it.

604
00:36:18,814 --> 00:36:19,749
Grandma.

605
00:36:22,418 --> 00:36:23,252
Oh.

606
00:36:23,953 --> 00:36:25,254
Itsuki.

607
00:36:26,389 --> 00:36:27,923
The doctor told me…

608
00:36:29,058 --> 00:36:32,728
"Your grandmother did her best.
She's going to be fine now."

609
00:36:33,763 --> 00:36:34,830
I see.

610
00:36:37,166 --> 00:36:40,903
I'm sorry for making you worry.

611
00:36:44,206 --> 00:36:45,775
What are you saying?

612
00:36:49,045 --> 00:36:51,080
I'm the one who should apologize.

613
00:36:54,884 --> 00:36:56,385
I'm sorry, Grandma.

614
00:37:00,289 --> 00:37:01,957
I'm sorry.

615
00:37:02,024 --> 00:37:03,859
I'm sorry.

616
00:37:03,926 --> 00:37:06,896
I'm sorry…

617
00:37:06,962 --> 00:37:09,598
-Sorry…
-You've always been…

618
00:37:10,366 --> 00:37:12,868
such a crybaby.

619
00:37:19,709 --> 00:37:21,143
By any chance,

620
00:37:22,178 --> 00:37:25,047
are you his homeroom teacher?

621
00:37:25,114 --> 00:37:26,716
Oh, well…

622
00:37:28,084 --> 00:37:32,788
You know, you can say that,
but I'm not sure… Right?

623
00:37:33,456 --> 00:37:35,324
Please don't pass it to me.

624
00:37:35,391 --> 00:37:36,325
Sorry.

625
00:37:37,393 --> 00:37:40,930
I'm happy to meet you.

626
00:37:42,365 --> 00:37:45,501
Please take good care of my grandson.

627
00:37:46,068 --> 00:37:48,137
I entrust him to you.

628
00:37:50,005 --> 00:37:51,040
Yes, ma'am.

629
00:37:56,379 --> 00:37:57,413
See you.

630
00:37:58,547 --> 00:37:59,615
Hey, Itsuki,

631
00:38:00,516 --> 00:38:02,418
come back to our class.

632
00:38:03,719 --> 00:38:04,754
What?

633
00:38:05,821 --> 00:38:07,423
We're always waiting for you.

634
00:38:11,594 --> 00:38:12,428
Well, then.

635
00:38:14,630 --> 00:38:15,798
Mr. Onizuka…

636
00:38:19,034 --> 00:38:20,970
Why did you choose this job?

637
00:38:30,012 --> 00:38:31,781
Isn't it obvious?

638
00:38:32,815 --> 00:38:34,717
Because I want to stay at school.

639
00:38:36,152 --> 00:38:37,219
Besides,

640
00:38:37,853 --> 00:38:42,258
I get to talk a lot
with young folks like you.

641
00:38:54,670 --> 00:38:57,807
CLASS 1-A

642
00:39:00,075 --> 00:39:01,143
Hey!

643
00:39:02,144 --> 00:39:03,679
Good morning, Itsuki.

644
00:39:03,746 --> 00:39:06,449
I heard from Onicchi,
your grandma went through a lot, right?

645
00:39:07,082 --> 00:39:07,917
Oh.

646
00:39:08,717 --> 00:39:09,585
Yes.

647
00:39:10,252 --> 00:39:11,821
If there's anything I can do,

648
00:39:12,521 --> 00:39:13,622
just say the word.

649
00:39:13,689 --> 00:39:15,224
I'm not sure you can do anything.

650
00:39:16,091 --> 00:39:18,427
Why don't we go visit your grandma today?

651
00:39:18,494 --> 00:39:20,196
Oh! Ni-i!

652
00:39:20,262 --> 00:39:22,298
Oh, did you mean "nice idea"?

653
00:39:23,065 --> 00:39:25,468
Tell us where
the hospital is later, Itsuki.

654
00:39:27,970 --> 00:39:29,205
Sure.

655
00:39:29,271 --> 00:39:30,272
Thanks.

656
00:39:30,339 --> 00:39:31,340
Bye then!

657
00:39:31,407 --> 00:39:32,741
-See you later.
-Later!

658
00:39:34,243 --> 00:39:36,846
Hey, are we doing
after-school study today?

659
00:39:36,912 --> 00:39:38,147
We are.

660
00:39:38,214 --> 00:39:39,548
Of course we are!

661
00:39:40,115 --> 00:39:40,983
What's wrong?

662
00:39:41,517 --> 00:39:42,418
Hurry and come in.

663
00:39:43,586 --> 00:39:44,453
Right.

664
00:39:45,087 --> 00:39:45,921
Okay.

665
00:39:47,223 --> 00:39:48,057
Excuse me…

666
00:39:51,126 --> 00:39:53,195
Do you watch videos at 2x speed too?

667
00:39:54,830 --> 00:39:57,099
I don't want to waste time.
Why do you ask?

668
00:39:57,666 --> 00:39:58,501
No reason…

669
00:39:59,969 --> 00:40:00,870
Then,

670
00:40:02,137 --> 00:40:04,807
why did you choose this job?

671
00:40:06,041 --> 00:40:07,243
That's because…

672
00:40:09,111 --> 00:40:12,214
I want to solve the problems
you students are facing,

673
00:40:12,748 --> 00:40:14,850
and help you get into your target schools.

674
00:40:17,553 --> 00:40:18,487
I see.

675
00:40:18,554 --> 00:40:21,023
Let's have another productive day.

676
00:40:23,292 --> 00:40:24,360
Oh, by the way…

677
00:40:24,860 --> 00:40:25,594
What?

678
00:40:26,362 --> 00:40:29,198
My grandma's okay now. She made it.

679
00:40:29,899 --> 00:40:31,333
Sorry for causing you worry.

680
00:40:32,468 --> 00:40:34,403
I see, that's good to hear.

681
00:40:38,240 --> 00:40:40,342
Good morning, everyone.

682
00:40:42,044 --> 00:40:43,946
Are you tired, Mr. Onizuka?

683
00:40:44,013 --> 00:40:46,282
Sorry. I didn't sleep enough…

684
00:40:46,815 --> 00:40:47,650
But…

685
00:40:48,250 --> 00:40:51,554
Looks like today
is going to be a good day.

686
00:40:51,620 --> 00:40:53,022
What? Why?

687
00:40:53,088 --> 00:40:54,256
Itsuki…

688
00:40:54,757 --> 00:40:57,459
will be back soon. Back to our class.

689
00:40:57,526 --> 00:40:59,261
Are you sure you should say that?

690
00:40:59,328 --> 00:41:00,296
It's fine.

691
00:41:01,530 --> 00:41:03,198
According to my gut feeling,

692
00:41:03,265 --> 00:41:05,868
in five seconds,
he will walk in through the door!

693
00:41:06,635 --> 00:41:08,704
Let's start the countdown.

694
00:41:09,772 --> 00:41:10,706
Five.

695
00:41:11,707 --> 00:41:12,775
Four.

696
00:41:13,342 --> 00:41:14,376
Three.

697
00:41:15,444 --> 00:41:16,645
Two.

698
00:41:17,546 --> 00:41:18,547
One!

699
00:41:19,181 --> 00:41:20,316
Zero!

700
00:41:23,319 --> 00:41:24,153
What?

701
00:41:24,720 --> 00:41:26,055
I don't see him.

702
00:41:26,121 --> 00:41:29,325
No, that can't be…

703
00:41:29,825 --> 00:41:31,794
CLASS 1-B

704
00:41:33,162 --> 00:41:34,263
No way?

705
00:41:49,211 --> 00:41:50,179
Hey.

706
00:41:51,013 --> 00:41:51,880
Itsuki!

707
00:41:54,817 --> 00:41:55,818
Are you okay?

708
00:41:57,953 --> 00:41:58,887
Sorry!

709
00:41:59,655 --> 00:42:02,124
I was about to enter,
and before I knew it…

710
00:42:06,128 --> 00:42:07,162
Here.

711
00:42:24,079 --> 00:42:25,381
Sorry, everyone.

712
00:42:26,148 --> 00:42:28,550
I caused some trouble, but I'm back.

713
00:42:30,486 --> 00:42:32,621
Let's get along again!

714
00:42:41,563 --> 00:42:42,765
That's why my nickname…

715
00:42:44,366 --> 00:42:46,602
will be "Comeback!"

716
00:42:50,272 --> 00:42:52,141
Got it. Comeback.

717
00:43:06,088 --> 00:43:11,427
All right, now our class
is a perfect number again!

718
00:43:18,934 --> 00:43:21,270
See you tomorrow!

719
00:43:22,871 --> 00:43:23,706
Mr. Onizuka.

720
00:43:25,607 --> 00:43:28,377
That was good.
Everything worked out well again.

721
00:43:28,444 --> 00:43:29,445
Right.

722
00:43:29,978 --> 00:43:31,714
I feel like…

723
00:43:31,780 --> 00:43:35,784
I might actually be able
to stay at this school until retirement.

724
00:43:35,851 --> 00:43:36,985
Right…

725
00:43:37,052 --> 00:43:38,854
I hope you can, but…

726
00:43:38,921 --> 00:43:40,155
But what?

727
00:43:40,222 --> 00:43:43,759
Well, the online message board…

728
00:43:43,826 --> 00:43:45,828
-There has been another post.
-Oh?

729
00:43:46,595 --> 00:43:48,964
IF YOU GET COCKY,
CLASS 1-B WILL FACE A DISASTER

730
00:43:49,031 --> 00:43:52,534
Oh well. This kind of stuff
is just hogwash. Don't worry about it.

731
00:43:52,601 --> 00:43:55,471
You say that, but these posts
have been right every time.

732
00:43:55,537 --> 00:43:56,872
Well, yeah.

733
00:43:56,939 --> 00:43:58,741
-Cover the back!
-Go right, right!

734
00:43:59,942 --> 00:44:01,944
Pass from behind! Behind!

735
00:44:06,582 --> 00:44:10,052
-Circle around and…
-Hiroto's always so cool, huh.

736
00:44:10,119 --> 00:44:11,053
Don't pass it back!

737
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:14,022
If I remember right,
he's here on a soccer scholarship.

738
00:44:15,324 --> 00:44:19,261
With him around, we might just win
the next high school soccer tournament.

739
00:44:19,328 --> 00:44:20,529
Wow…

740
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:23,031
Hey, do your best, Hiroto!

741
00:44:25,701 --> 00:44:26,935
Hiroto!

742
00:44:42,184 --> 00:44:43,418
Hiroto!

743
00:44:48,590 --> 00:44:49,525
You old bastard!

744
00:44:49,591 --> 00:44:52,161
Try saying that one more time, punk!

745
00:44:52,227 --> 00:44:53,462
<i>I'm quitting the soccer team!</i>

746
00:44:53,529 --> 00:44:54,463
<i>Get out of here!</i>

747
00:44:54,530 --> 00:44:55,264
A hypocrite.

748
00:44:56,498 --> 00:44:58,133
-Hey!
-Watch out!

749
00:44:58,200 --> 00:45:00,335
How about a toast, with this?

750
00:45:00,402 --> 00:45:03,405
She truly believes
in the power of education.

751
00:45:03,472 --> 00:45:05,240
Did you cause trouble again?

752
00:45:05,307 --> 00:45:07,442
Weed, or gummies…

753
00:45:07,509 --> 00:45:09,378
<i>It's because he has a father like you</i>

754
00:45:09,444 --> 00:45:13,148
<i>that Hiroto grew up to be someone</i>
<i>who doesn't understand people's feelings!</i>

755
00:45:13,215 --> 00:45:16,151
<i>Hiroto's life is his and his alone.</i>

756
00:45:16,218 --> 00:45:17,186
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

